WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.420
It's time for "Dear Drew"

2
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.650
and we have a very special guest joining us today.

3
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.390
He is known for playing Kevin G,

4
00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:10.820
the rapping mathlete in "Mean Girls"

5
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.600
and he's also made a name for himself on Instagram,

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.990
displaying his calligraphy art with pen pals,

7
00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.730
he has all around the country.

8
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.680
Please welcome the creator of "Letters in Ink,"

9
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.724
Rajiv Surendra.

10
00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:28.724
(audience cheering)

11
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:40.067
We here at "Dear Drew" usually start the segment with,

12
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.230
we call it the Zip Code of the Day.

13
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.583
And today's zip code is 27606,

14
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.980
Raleigh, North Carolina.

15
00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:50.813
That's right.

16
00:00:50.813 --> 00:00:53.097
(audience applauding)

17
00:00:53.097 --> 00:00:56.153
And it is home of our affiliate station,

18
00:00:56.153 --> 00:00:59.450
WRAZ Fox 50.

19
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:04.060
Home to more than 40 free historic attractions and museums,

20
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.950
Raleigh is also known as the Smithsonian of the South.

21
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:08.890
That's cool.

22
00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.140
From paintings to pints, the Raleigh Beer Garden

23
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.320
in the Guinness Book of World Records,

24
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.290
has the largest selection of beers on tap

25
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:20.250
with over 360 to choose from.

26
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.320
Cheers.

27
00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.690
Cheers to you, Raleigh.

28
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.100
North Carolina, we would love to hear from you.

29
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.526
Please write us a letter.

30
00:01:26.526 --> 00:01:29.700
(audience applauding)

31
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.533
All right.

32
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.190
Let's open our first letter.

33
00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.570
Ooh, this is more than a letter.

34
00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.780
Ooh, I am loving this already.

35
00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.860
I'm a tie-dye sock enthusiast!

36
00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.240
This person gets me, they know me.

37
00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.080
Dear Drew,

38
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.680
I couldn't think of anyone that loves flowers

39
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.960
as much as I do, besides you.

40
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.350
Enclosed are a few items

41
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.070
that have been naturally dyed using flowers

42
00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.550
and botanicals that I make

43
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:59.620
and sell online at michellemooredesigns.com.

44
00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.490
Michelle. Kingston, New York.

45
00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:02.323
Oh.

46
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:04.653
That's so beautiful.

47
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.950
Okay. These are incredible.

48
00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.080
I really am, by the way, Michelle,

49
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.100
a huge tie-dye sock enthusiast

50
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.890
and the fact that it came from flowers is so romantic.

51
00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:17.750
I mean,

52
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:18.583
wow!

53
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:22.329
And we're gonna put your store on our website,

54
00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:24.210
michellemooredesigns.com

55
00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.960
so that we can feature you

56
00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.260
in our "Little Book of Small Businesses Gift Guide."

57
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.490
Rajiv, your letter.

58
00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.790
(paper crinkling)

59
00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:34.910
Hi Rajiv,

60
00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.160
I had the greatest pleasure

61
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.950
of discovering your "Letter Writing is Not Dead" video.

62
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.700
There is something truly magical

63
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.690
and sentimental about writing someone a letter.

64
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.900
Jamil. Harrison, New Jersey.

65
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.010
Oh, I love that.

66
00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:50.944
Oh, Jamil.

67
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:54.194
(audience applauding)

68
00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:00.560
How does it feel that this is really taking off

69
00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.810
and connecting people?

70
00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.420
I'm so honored.

71
00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.230
I have been handwriting since I was a little kid

72
00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.220
and it turned into calligraphy.

73
00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.370
The question that I get asked most often

74
00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.030
is how do I start to learn calligraphy?

75
00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.290
Will you teach me something?

76
00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.760
Because I've never done it.

77
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.860
Shall we do a little demo?
Yeah.

78
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.723
Shall I show you a little something?

79
00:03:20.723 --> 00:03:22.220
Yes.
Okay.

80
00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.308
So we're gonna start by just like a stretch.

81
00:03:25.308 --> 00:03:28.660
(audience laughing)

82
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:29.830
I want you to move your arms,

83
00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:30.930
move your arms.

84
00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.230
Exactly.

85
00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.202
Exactly. Okay, now let's take it to the board.

86
00:03:34.202 --> 00:03:36.320
(audience cheering)

87
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.570
So this is what we're gonna do.

88
00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:38.610
We're gonna make ovals

89
00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.640
but we're gonna make them on us on a 52 degrees slant.

90
00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.660
So watch me.

91
00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.760
We're just gonna go like this and use your whole arm.

92
00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.177
(chalk scratching board)

93
00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.840
Good.

94
00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:53.270
So once you've kind of loosened up,

95
00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.800
we're gonna go to our letter forms.

96
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.760
Okay.

97
00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.040
Let's do a D.
Okay.

98
00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:57.873
So watch me.

99
00:03:57.873 --> 00:04:00.773
We're gonna start with a stroke that goes down.

100
00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.800
I'm gonna make a little loop.

101
00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.453
I'm gonna go down and then up and down.

102
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.580
Nice!

103
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:14.683
And now let's put in the R-E-W.

104
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:16.640
Nice.

105
00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.110
If you keep practicing, let me show you

106
00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.470
what it will look like

107
00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.370
in a few years, okay?
All right, yeah, you-

108
00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.567
I'm gonna show you.

109
00:04:23.909 --> 00:04:27.326
(chalk scratching board)

110
00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.764
I ran out of room, but-

111
00:04:36.764 --> 00:04:39.764
(audience cheering)

112
00:04:43.668 --> 00:04:44.829
Don't look, turn around.

113
00:04:44.829 --> 00:04:46.700
Okay. Let's turn around.

114
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.936
Lets do our separate versions of it.

115
00:04:48.936 --> 00:04:52.870
(chalk scratching board)

116
00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:53.920
That's my signature.

117
00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.450
Look how beautiful that is.

118
00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.690
Oh my God.

119
00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.523
This is so special.

120
00:04:57.523 --> 00:04:58.680
(audience cheering)

121
00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.138
Ow.

122
00:05:00.138 --> 00:05:00.971
All right.

123
00:05:00.971 --> 00:05:02.297
We've got one more letter

124
00:05:02.297 --> 00:05:04.910
and this one is from Linda

125
00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.663
from Sudbury, Massachusetts.

126
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.300
I wanted to write you to thank you for developing your show.

127
00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.630
I'm a 74 year old grandmother who lives alone

128
00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.280
and you brought much comical fun, and happiness to my life.

129
00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.140
P.S. Yellow is my favorite color too.

130
00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:26.190
See by a few pictures of my yellow belongings.

131
00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.563
Linda. Sudbury, Massachusetts.

132
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.327
Oh, look at her beautiful-

133
00:05:31.327 --> 00:05:32.205
(audience sighing)

134
00:05:32.205 --> 00:05:33.415
Oh!

135
00:05:33.415 --> 00:05:36.665
(audience applauding)

136
00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:45.470
I mean, I didn't know what she was gonna say

137
00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.230
but we are gonna actually surprise her on Zoom.

138
00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:52.130
She thinks she's gonna talk to a producer from our show

139
00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.390
but we're gonna surprise her.

140
00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.332
Nice!

141
00:05:54.332 --> 00:05:55.920
High five.
Nice!

142
00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:56.753
Okay.

143
00:05:56.753 --> 00:05:59.836
(audience cheering)

144
00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.711
Hello, Linda. Are you there?

145
00:06:04.711 --> 00:06:06.423
I am. Hi, Drew!

146
00:06:08.455 --> 00:06:09.312
Hi, Linda!

147
00:06:09.312 --> 00:06:12.395
(audience cheering)

148
00:06:14.861 --> 00:06:16.170
Oh, Linda!

149
00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:19.280
You look so beautiful with your yellow beads

150
00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.923
and your yellow shirt.

151
00:06:22.165 --> 00:06:24.122
And my yellow glass

152
00:06:24.122 --> 00:06:25.916
and my yellow phone.

153
00:06:25.916 --> 00:06:26.969
Wow.

154
00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:29.295
Oh, I'm so happy to meet you!

155
00:06:29.295 --> 00:06:30.128
Ah.

156
00:06:30.128 --> 00:06:35.128
Linda, I have this basket of yellow swag from our show,

157
00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.800
but if it's okay,

158
00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.650
you'll have to come by and get it.

159
00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:43.370
So we would love to bring you and your best girlfriend

160
00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.540
to a taping of the show right here in the city

161
00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.040
and include you in the show

162
00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.230
and have you be our special guests.

163
00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.390
And then afterwards, we wanna send you out

164
00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.850
to a fabulous, fancy dinner in the city.

165
00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.353
Oh, and a spa too.

166
00:06:57.513 --> 00:07:00.596
(audience cheering)

167
00:07:05.945 --> 00:07:08.480 line:15%
Okay. Michelle, Linda, and Jamil.

168
00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:11.020 line:15%
Thank you for your letters so much.

169
00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:13.870 line:15%
Here are our postcards to you

170
00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.520 line:15%
